Link Tunnel job: The motorway may have to be built largely underground. Photo: NSW Government
Infrastructure NSW, the O'Farrell government's advisory body, promoted the idea last year as a means of reducing the price of the project, which it said would cost about $10 billion.
It said the sunken motorway would look like a boulevard in Paris or Barcelona, and also compared the idea to Sydney's existing open-cut Eastern Distributor.
Advertisement
But officials working on the project have since been told the slot would be more expensive than a tunnel and are understood to have adopted the advice.
This is because the government would have had to buy up and tear down large amounts of property for about five kilometres on either side of Parramatta Road west of Taverners Hill, near Petersham.
